<title>CHILE: Chile Central Bank eases restrictions on banks.</title>
<headline>Chile Central Bank eases restrictions on banks.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's Central Bank said on Thursday it would allow commercial banks to finance trade deals between two countries outside of Chile.</p>
<p>&quot;The Central Bank...has decided to authorize national banks, in a first stage, to finance foreign trade operations&quot; between other countries,&quot; said the bank in a statement.</p>
<p>Banks would be able to grant loans to individuals and companies resident abroad to carry out operations in countries other than Chile, it said.</p>
<p>The measure will be published in the government gazette Diario Oficial on April 12.</p>
</text>
